Z||000018||Cozmo||07-03-2001||08:37 AM||||No Roy, no turbo pics, maybe someone else got some but I didn't.  It was mounted next to the trunk where the alt./coil cooling stuff used to be.  Some really weird exhaust plumbing, lots of heat wrap and some BIG heat shields (kinda homemade looking).  Yes it was for sale, no we didn't find out how much...(BOO!) <BR>The reason there is no color in the lineup pic is YOU weren't there MrFixit58!!!<BR>(Roy's our clubs' "true blue" Fiero) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>BTW fierobaby, I had a very attractive bright green tarp over my Targa (about in the middle of the line) because it was raining and I had left the top in the garage. Does that count???  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>   The place is a combo sales /museum, about half the cars weren't for sale tho.  Tarpon Springs is a good trip, if anyone gets the chance it's worth the effort to check out.  We ate at Pappas, world renown Greek cuisine and yes, it was SUPERB!<BR>Maybe we'll go to Don "Big Daddy" Garlits museum next...it's within a day trip...<BR><B>C02M0</B>||||reg||1
